.TH "RAPTOR-ADVISE" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-advise \- Check each MODEL for things a reliability engineer would question: redundancy that cannot work, placeholder data, spares or crews that cannot meet demand, maintenance that cannot pay off, too few runs. Nothing is run and nothing is changed. Each finding has a stable rule id and says whether it is exact or an estimate.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor advise\fR [\-h] [\-f {text,json,md}] [\-\-min\-severity {error,warning,advice,info}] [\-\-only IDS] [\-\-skip IDS] [\-\-why] [\-\-strict] [\-\-simulate] [\-\-target EXPR] [\-j N] [\-\-progress {auto,bar,json,none}] [\-\-list\-rules] [MODEL ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check each MODEL for things a reliability engineer would question: redundancy that cannot work, placeholder data, spares or crews that cannot meet demand, maintenance that cannot pay off, too few runs. Nothing is run and nothing is changed. Each finding has a stable rule id and says whether it is exact or an estimate.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json|md}\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-min\-severity\fR \fI{error|warning|advice|info}\fR
hide findings below this level (default: show all)
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fIIDS\fR
comma list of rule ids or prefixes to run, e.g. M\-SPR,M\-PM\-003
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR \fIIDS\fR
comma list of rule ids or prefixes to leave out
.TP
\fB\-\-why\fR
print the reasoning under each finding (text format)
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
exit 3 on warnings as well as errors
.TP
\fB\-\-simulate\fR
also run each model with its own settings and say how far to trust the results
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fIEXPR\fR
a requirement to judge the run against, e.g. 'system.ao>=0.995' (implies \-\-simulate; repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
worker processes for \-\-simulate (default 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI{auto|bar|json|none}\fR
progress of \-\-simulate on stderr (json: one object per line)
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-rules\fR
list every rule and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
List what looks wrong or unwise, most important first.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor advise plant.rbds\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Leave out the notes and print the reasoning under each finding.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor advise plant.rbds \-\-why \-\-min\-severity advice\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Only the spares and resource checks, machine\-readable.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor advise plant.rbds \-\-only M\-SPR,M\-RES \-f json\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run the model and say whether the target is met, missed or too close to call.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor advise plant.rbds \-\-target 'system.ao>=0.995'\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Every rule, its level and its method.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor advise \-\-list\-rules\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
success
.TP
\fB1\fR
runtime error
.TP
\fB2\fR
usage error
.TP
\fB3\fR
model invalid (validation errors)
.TP
\fB4\fR
model refused: a shape that cannot be run
.TP
\fB5\fR
timed out or aborted; partial results written
.TP
\fB6\fR
output could not be written
.TP
\fB130\fR
interrupted (Ctrl\-C); partial results written
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_DEBUG\fR
same as \-\-debug
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_DEV_FEATURES\fR
same as \-\-dev\-features
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_CONFIG\fR
path of the settings file (same as \-\-config)
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_WORKSPACE\fR
default for \-\-workspace
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_SEED\fR
salt for every random stream (same as \-\-seed)
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
disable colour output
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME\fR
base directories
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/raptor\-studio/config.toml\fR
settings file (see raptor\-config(5))
.TP
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/raptor\-studio/mcp\fR
default MCP server workspace
